# Flush if there's no Gap -- confirmed with the user rather than guessed
# at, since an analysis with both attached has no way to know which one
# an already-uploaded photo was "for". A row on an analysis with neither
# Gap nor Flush attached (possible before this feature existed, since
# the gallery used to show regardless of whether either entry existed)
# has nothing to backfill onto and is deleted, along with its MinIO
# object -- it could never be reached through either gallery afterwards
